hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15937","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us from his book, he said, Ibn Lahi'a informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Hubayra, from Hassan ibn Kurayb: that a boy of theirs died, and his parents grieved severely over him. So Hawshab, the Companion of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), said: Shall I not inform you of what I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say concerning the like of your son? That a man of his Companions had a son who had grown up or begun to walk, and he used to come with his father to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then his son died, and his father grieved over him for nearly six days, not coming to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I do not see so-and-so. They said: O Messenger of Allah, his son died and he grieved over him. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: O so-and-so, would you love that your son be with you now as the most active of boys in activity? Would you love that your son be with you as the boldest of youths in boldness? Would you love that your son be with you grown as the best of grown men? Or that it be said to you: Enter Paradise as reward for what was taken from you?"
